 their vocal tract and replaces the air that would normally be there.\n4. Helium has a lower density than air, which causes sound waves to travel faster through it.\n5. As a result, the pitch of the voice increases when a person speaks or sings with helium.\n6. The pitch of a voice is determined by the frequency of the sound waves produced by the vocal cords.\n7. A higher pitch means a higher frequency, while a lower pitch means a lower frequency.\n8. Therefore, speaking with helium actually makes the voice sound higher-pitched, not deeper.", "new_cot_probs": [3.392579328576062e-09, 1.2078418194505502e-06], "cot_prob": [-55.0], "cot_step_prob": [-63.0]}}}
