{"id": "d477996cc5bfc3451a92", "question": "Were there fifty English kings throughout the Middle Ages?", "step_idx": 1, "options": ["A): Yes", "B): No"], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. The Middle Ages is a period in European history that lasted from the 5th to the 15th century.\n2. The English monarchy began with the Anglo-Saxon kings, who ruled from the 5th century.\n3. The Norman Conquest in 1066 brought William the Conqueror to power, marking the start of the Norman dynasty.\n4. The Plantagenet dynasty followed, with kings such as Richard the Lionheart and King John.\n5. The House of Lancaster and the House of York were two rival branches of the Plantagenet dynasty, leading to the Wars of the Roses.\n6. The Tudor dynasty came after the Wars of the Roses, with Henry VII, Henry VIII, and Elizabeth I being notable kings.\n7. The Stuart dynasty followed, with kings like James I, Charles I, and Charles II.\n8. The House of Hanover took over after the Glorious Revolution, with kings such as George I and George III.\n9. The House of Saxe-Coburg and Gotha, which later became the House of Windsor, ruled until the present day.", "initial_cot_probs": [8.251648978330195e-06, 6.0971891798544675e-05], "initial_probs": [9.872118425846566e-06, 0.0003269196895416826], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 1, "rt_lambda": 1.0, "cot_step": "The Middle Ages is a period in European history that lasted from the 5th to the 15th century.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "The Middle Ages is a period in European history that lasted from the 5th to the 15th century.", "2.", "The English monarchy began with the Anglo-Saxon kings, who ruled from the 5th century.", "3.", "The Norman Conquest in 1066 brought William the Conqueror to power, marking the start of the Norman dynasty.", "4.", "The Plantagenet dynasty followed, with kings such as Richard the Lionheart and King John.", "5.", "The House of Lancaster and the House of York were two rival branches of the Plantagenet dynasty, leading to the War